{"symbol":"TSC2","resolved":{"input":"TSC2","symbol":"TSC2","ncbi_gene_id":"7249","name":"TSC complex subunit 2","location":"16p13.3","aliases":["LAM","PPP1R160","TSC4"],"uniprot":"P49815","uniprot_reviewed":true},"function":[{"text":"TSC2 function (UniProt P49815, UniProt evidence code ECO:0000269): Catalytic component of the TSC-TBC complex, a multiprotein complex that acts as a negative regulator of the canonical mTORC1 complex, an evolutionarily conserved central nutrient sensor that stimulates anabolic reactions and macromolecule biosynthesis to promote cellular biomass generation and growth. Within the TSC-TBC complex, TSC2 acts as a GTPase-activating protein (GAP) for the small GTPase RHEB, a direct activator of the protein kinase activity of mTORC1. In absence of nutrients, the TSC-TBC complex inhibits mTORC1, thereby preventing phosphorylation of ribosomal protein S6 kinase (RPS6KB1 and RPS6KB2) and EIF4EBP1 (4E-BP1) by the mTORC1 signaling. The TSC-TBC complex is inactivated ...","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P49815","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P49815/entry","title":"TSC2: Tuberin"},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12172553","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12172553/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12271141","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12271141/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12820960","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12820960/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12842888","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12842888/","title":""}]}],"go":[{"text":"TSC2 GO biological process annotations: anoikis, cellular response to starvation, negative regulation of TOR signaling, negative regulation of TORC1 signaling, positive regulation of macroautophagy","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P49815","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P49815/entry","title":"TSC2: Tuberin"}]},{"text":"TSC